<title>GERMANY: HEW plans to raise 96 dividend to 20 pct.</title>
<headline>HEW plans to raise 96 dividend to 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electricity group Hamburgische Electricitaets-Werke AG said on Wednesday that it planned to raise its dividend on 1996 earnings to 20 percent from 17 percent.</p>
<p>In a mandatory bourse statement, the group also announced that it had posted a net profit of 127.9 million marks last year. Of that amount 36 million marks will be put into reserves and 92.2 million marks will be paid out in dividends.</p>
<p>The group said it planned to pay a dividend of 10 marks per share per share nominally valued at 50 marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
